cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. It is unrefereed and was produced largely with AI assistance (see README.md)."
title: "A certified simple, even ground state of the localized Weil quadratic form for all windows L in (0, 1.4035]"
abstract: "Computer-assisted proof, in Arb ball arithmetic, that the lowest eigenvalue of the localized Weil quadratic form for the Riemann zeta function on L^2(-L, L) is simple with an even eigenfunction for every L in (0, 1.4035]. Pieces I-II cover (0, 1.19] (release of 2026-10-26); Piece III covers [1.19, 1.4035] with second-eigenvalue lower bounds from Elston's certifier plus a rank-one deflation and rigorous Legendre-Galerkin upper bounds. Interim release: the extension to L = 1.5 is in progress and not claimed. Unrefereed; produced largely with AI assistance."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Johann Alexander"
    family-names: "Botha"
    email: "info@genuscore.com"
version: "1.1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Weil explicit formula
  - Riemann zeta function
  - computer-assisted proof
  - interval arithmetic
  - Arb
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Weil positivity in compact windows: a finite reduction, certified two-sided bounds, and a Landau-Widom decay law"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhu
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2608.24827"
    notes: "The reduction strategy used by every window certificate; certified simple-even at L = 0.8."
  - type: article
    title: "Arb: efficient arbitrary-precision midpoint-radius interval arithmetic"
    authors:
      - family-names: Johansson
        given-names: Fredrik
    journal: "IEEE Transactions on Computers"
    volume: 66
